        "ratings": [
            {
                "comment": "This class has many assigned readings, but I only read two of the books; not the textbook or online readings, and got an A. Lectures are interesting, and the guest lecturers made the class unique as you got to learn from more than one professor. There are no exams, only papers. The expectations are clear and if you follow them you will do well.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Fair had interesting lectures, clear grading outlines and a few extra credit opportunities.",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Fair is definitely very knowledgeable on all things Africa. Going from pre-colonial history to modern youth culture, this class covers a lot. There is a lot of assigned online reading but it's not always necessary; she lectures from an outline and her memory, so attending lecture is important. Grading is on three papers (75%) and discussion.",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Fair not only is extremely knowledgeable about the topic, but her passion for it makes it that much more exciting.  Probably one of the best teachers I've ever had- plus the topic is super interesting.  Take this class with her!",
                "difficulty_rating": 4,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "This course is kind of a sm\u00f6rg\u00e5sbord of random topics about media effects. Prof. Fair keeps it interesting...especially her lecture on****. She's quirky and accessible, but she has no overhead notes and just talks from memory, so going to lecture is a must. Exams are clearly outlined. 2 exams, 1 paper and lots of points for discussion section.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 3
            }
